{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-447461-r4505779","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Nigerian Wheatbread Toast","sourcePageId":447461,"sourceRevision":"4505779","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-10T01:42:23Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Nigerian%20Wheatbread%20Toast&oldid=4505779","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:09:29.172Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:National Nigerian recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using bread","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using cucumber","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using lettuce","Category:Recipes using onion","Category:Recipes using pepper","Category:Recipes using salt","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"b17d191851e07a15d1be195c76b68d44d72e27e0cb5bef5fdf5fe9a4d5364c86","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Nigerian recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{Recipe}}\n\nThis is a type of toast that is made with wheat bread. It can be served as a breakfast or snack.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n* [[Cookbook:Egg|Egg]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* Sliced wheat [[Cookbook:Bread|bread]]\n* [[Cookbook:Butter|Butter]]\n* [[Cookbook:Oil and Fat|Oil]]\n* Yellow pepper powder\n* [[Cookbook:Pepper|Black pepper]] powder\n* [[Cookbook:Lettuce|Lettuce]]\n* [[Cookbook:Onion|Onions]], [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]]\n* [[Cookbook:Cucumber|Cucumber]], sliced\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# Crack the egg, and [[Cookbook:Whisk|whisk]] it with a [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] of salt.\n# Spread some butter on the bread slices.\n# Spread some of the beaten egg on each slice of bread. Do not add so much egg that the bread is soaked.\n# Heat a [[Cookbook:Non-stick|nonstick]] [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|pan]] over low heat, and add a thin layer of butter or oil.\n# Place the bread slices in the pan egg-side down. Sprinkle with yellow and black pepper.\n# Cook over low heat until the bread is dry and crisp. Remove from the heat.\n# Top the toast with the lettuce and sliced vegetables.\n\n[[Category:National Nigerian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cucumber]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bread]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lettuce]]\n[[Category:Recipes using onion]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Nigerian Wheatbread Toast","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"Egg","sourceText":"Egg","amountText":"Egg","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"Salt","sourceText":"Salt","amountText":"Salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"Sliced wheat bread","sourceText":"Sliced wheat bread","amountText":"Sliced wheat bread","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"Butter","sourceText":"Butter","amountText":"Butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"Oil","sourceText":"Oil","amountText":"Oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"Yellow pepper p